                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Super underrated combat. 10/10\nVery good story. the plot kept me hooked, i couldn't stop playing it until i beat it.\n\nif you cannot launch the game, its because you do not have .net framework 3.5\nbelow is a super simple guide to get you playing watchmen in no time. \n\nyou will need .net framework 3.5 to run some older games like Watchmen, Batman, etc. \n\ngo to \"about this pc\" and figure out which windows you have. i have 26H1.\n \nhttps://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download/dotnet-framework/net35-sp1\nMicrosoft\nDownload .NET Framework 3.5 SP1 | .NET\n\nif you are worried about copy and pasting that link ( i get it ), just look up .net framework 3.5 download and visit the microsoft page, \n\ndownload the 3.5 standalone for the appropriate windows you have on your pc, mine is the first one. you only \nneed the standalone, not the language pack. follow the install process and restart pc\n\nat this point you can run the game but additionally, you can uncap your frames as well. the game is native for 60fps. go to nvidia control panel, manage 3d settings, program settings (next to global settings tab on the right), locate watchmen: the end is nigh, locate max fps under features and settings (box 3.) change the fps from global to on, set it to your monitors refresh rate (respectfully 10+ fps higher). scroll down to vertical sync in the same area (box 3.) and disable it.\n\nattempting to close the nvidia control panel after changes will prompt you to apply changes, do so.\nnow enjoy your super smooth watchmen and go beat up all the bad guys C:\n\ni just beat the game, super super good\ncrazy ending",
